# A fill rectangle into a 16-bit colour image whose width (289) is odd: its odd rows start on the odd halfword of a memory
# word, and the fill colour's half a pixel takes is the memory halfword's (the address's bit 1), not the column's: the
# oracle's first pixel of a row of that kind is the colour's low half. The model took the column's parity (every other
# row's halves swapped); the RTL left the last pixel of those rows out and shifted them by one pixel.
rdram zero
cmd 3f100120 00100000
cmd 2d000000 00484268
cmd 2f300000 00000000
cmd 37000000 f80107c1
cmd 36484268 00000000
cmd 37000000 1234cdef
cmd 36200100 00400048
cmd 29000000 00000000
